# Server settings. Every value below is fake.
#
# Local development needs none of these: `npm run dev`, `npm run build`,
# `npm run test:e2e` and the unit tests use PGlite, a Postgres that runs inside
# Node, with no account or Docker. To set one locally, copy the line into
# `.env.local` (git ignores it) and remove the `#`. Never commit real values.

# Which deployment this is: local (the default), staging or production.
# Staging and production refuse to start without DATABASE_URL and
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, and production also refuses the fake SMS provider. On
# Vercel it must be staging or production (task 20 sets it there).
# APP_ENV=production

# A Postgres connection URL, starting with postgres:// or postgresql://.
# When it is set, the app uses that database in every mode, and does not
# migrate or seed it. Server only: never add a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://gomechanic:fake-password@localhost:5432/gomechanic

# Signs the login cookie: at least 32 random characters. Required on staging
# and production (make one with `openssl rand -base64 32`). Locally a fixed
# placeholder is used. Server only: never add a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=fake-secret-replace-with-32-or-more-random-characters

# Who sends SMS: fake (the default, and the only choice until task 44) stores
# them for the /dev/outbox page. Production refuses fake.
# SMS_PROVIDER=fake

# The browser tests set this themselves (playwright.config.ts): the fake SMS
# provider also writes each message to this file. Local runs only.
# E2E_OUTBOX_FILE=/path/to/outbox.jsonl
